      "hints": [
        "Express arc lengths as $r\\alpha$ and $2r\\alpha$.",
        "Note that the two straight boundary segments each have length $2r - r = r$.",
        "Sum the four sides, equate to $4.4r$, and solve for $\\alpha$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Express the lengths of the two circular arcs and the two straight radial segments:\n$$\\text{Arc } AB = r\\alpha, \\quad \\text{Arc } CD = 2r\\alpha$$\n$$AC = BD = 2r - r = r$$",
        "Equate the total perimeter to $4.4r$:\n$$\\text{Perimeter} = r\\alpha + 2r\\alpha + r + r = 3r\\alpha + 2r = 4.4r$$",
        "Solve for the angle $\\alpha$ in radians:\n$$3r\\alpha = 2.4r \\implies 3\\alpha = 2.4 \\implies \\alpha = 0.8\\text{ radians}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Circular Measure": "Sets up perimeter equation $r\\alpha + 2r\\alpha + r + r = 4.4r$ (M1). Solves for $\\alpha = 0.8$ radians (A1)."
